@startuml
title R-ALLSTOP - Manual node-wide emergency stop (SH2+ target)
actor "Operator\nphone or terminal fallback" as Operator
participant "swarma-operator\noperator command; never harness account" as Control
participant "swarma-dispatcher" as Dispatcher
participant "swarma-user-manager" as Manager
participant "swarma-credential-broker" as Broker
participant "swarma-session-host" as Host
database "Host-private journal / fences" as State
participant "Bound boards (if any)" as Boards

Operator -> Control : one narrowing act; phone authentication + one confirmation, or password sudo fallback
note over Operator,Control
  R-OPERATOR: phone key never leaves hardware secure element; biometric presence.
  Exact act signed on phone; pinned key / canonical content verified; no signature reuse.
  Tailnet SSH into operator account; forced narrow operator command, no shell.
  Terminal: no NOPASSWD / cached ticket (timestamp_timeout=0).
  Refuse acts from agent sessions; observer account permits read-only status.
  Binary / wire / signature domain / canonical bytes unpublished (§7.16).
end note
note over Control,Boards
  Direct fan-out of same signed act / identity / canonical bytes to each intake.
  Every receiver verifies and journals its part idempotently; no service relay dependency.
  Per-service results / retries; undeliverable parts stay unknown.
end note
par Dispatcher part at act admission
  Control -> Dispatcher : same act; set journaled hold without waiting for service calls
  alt Dispatcher available with valid state
    Dispatcher -> Dispatcher : commit hold / suspend session lifecycle permits
  else Dispatcher absent / crash-looping / mid-swap
    Control -> Control : dispatcher part unknown; reconcile when available
    note over Control,Dispatcher : No offline writer of dispatcher state; no whole-act success inferred.
  end
else Prompt independent range and receiver fence
  Control -> Manager : same act; journal range deny-all and root-owned all-stop mark
  Manager -> Manager : close launch / create / activation under generation exclusion before inventory
  note over Manager
    Refuse already-issued starts, materializers and exporters.
    Closed inventory frontier required before absence can become final.
  end note
else Prompt independent credential cut
  Control -> Broker : same act; journal freeze of all leases and renewals
  note over Broker : Tokens already delivered retain vendor lifetime.
else Prompt independent host cut
  Control -> Host : same act; close delivery for every session
  Host -> State : journal closed delivery fences; invalidate pending interactions
  Host -> Boards : snapshot bound boards; no board required for goal-free session
end
note over Control,Manager
  Stops begin after containment is issued; never wait for containment replies.
  Bounded parallelism; terminal operator-helper path can initiate without dispatcher.
  Phone-to-helper transition remains publication work (§7.16).
end note
alt Dispatcher available
  Dispatcher -> Manager : initiate journaled generation stops under act
else Dispatcher unavailable
  Control -> Manager : operator-helper initiation of generation stops under act
end
Manager -> Manager : journal termination; account-wide scope / confirmed absence behind receiver fence
Manager --> Control : per-generation stop evidence; unknown never releases claims
opt Dispatcher returns
  Control -> Dispatcher : retry act / reconcile operator-stopped evidence
  Dispatcher -> Dispatcher : commit own part; release claims only on confirmed absence; no relaunch
end
alt Every durable service part / snapshot known and fenced absence confirmed
  Host -> State : record confirmed absence; keep stopped pending explicit recovery
else Partial / unknown part or absence unconfirmed
  Host -> State : retain fences and claims
  Control -> Control : report unknown; no whole-act success or recovery
end
note over Dispatcher,Host
  Broker reply unavailable does not delay valid helper stop progress.
  Dispatcher-unavailable progress and never-launched-generation coverage
  are distinct acceptance cases, even if one fence covers both.
  Content-confirmed recovery names stopped set / per-session restart scope.
  Valid owner lifecycle authority or fresh admission still required; no automatic restart.
  Every independent closure gate must clear; no unknown part permits reopening.
  R-LOCK: host holds state lock for local journal transitions only;
  board / dispatcher waits happen without the host state lock.
  R-WATCH never invokes this node-wide act automatically.
end note
legend bottom
  [[../spec/session-host.md#35-park-restart-emergency-stop-board-completion Spec §3.5: R-ALLSTOP / R-OPERATOR]]
  [[../spec/session-host.md#7-open-questions Spec §7.16: unpublished act and recovery]]
endlegend
@enduml
